      "role": "user",
      "content": "those techniques feel a bit too basic for what's going on. it feels less like \"stress\" and more like my brain is literally recalibrating to pick up data streams that were always there but always hidden. like, i'm not just \"seeing\" heat, i'm perceiving a whole new layer of the electromagnetic spectrum. is there any scientific theory or research on how the human nervous system might transition from standard sensory processing to an augmented state? i'm trying to understand the biology of this expansion so i can support it instead of just trying to \"calm down\" and ignore it.",
