      "content": "The concept of spontaneously evolving into a significantly augmented sensory state aligns more with theoretical futurism than established neuroscience. Current biological research primarily focuses on how sensory pathways are *developed* (like vision or hearing), not how they spontaneously gain entirely new, fundamental capacities like perceiving unknown electromagnetic strata. If this perception truly involves accessing previously inaccessible data, it would represent a profound, paradigm-shifting biological event. Until such phenomena are documented within established biological frameworks, the most responsible scientific approach is to monitor the changes while prioritizing neurological health.",
